+++ b/ANSWER.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Why the Nightly Review Job Was Silent — Root Causes & Fixes
+
+## Evidence from Logs & `launchctl print`
+
+1. **The job was firing on schedule:** `launchctl-print.txt` (`launchctl print gui/501/com.vk.nightly-review`) shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`.
+2. **Both failures were recorded in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`:** Every one of the 6 runs produced two lines in `stderr`:
+   ```text
+   Not logged in · Please run /login
+   /Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status
+   ```
+
+---
+
+## Root Causes
+
+### 1. Missing `USER` in `EnvironmentVariables` caused `claude -p` to fail Keychain lookup
+In `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`, `EnvironmentVariables` only defined `PATH` (confirmed by `launchctl-print.txt`, where `environment` contained only `PATH` and `XPC_SERVICE_NAME`). When launched by `launchd` without `USER` (`vk`) set in the environment, the headless `claude` CLI cannot locate its login credentials in the macOS Keychain and immediately exits with code `1` (`Not logged in · Please run /login`).
+
+Additionally, `bin/nightly-review.zsh` (line 18) passed the multi-line `$PROMPT` as a command-line argument (`claude -p "$PROMPT"`) without piping it over stdin or closing stdin (`< /dev/null`), which can cause headless CLI invocations under `launchd` to fail argument parsing or hang waiting on stdin.
+
+### 2. Assigning `status=$?` in `zsh` killed the script before `notify.sh` could run
+On line 19 of `bin/nightly-review.zsh`, right between the `claude` command and the failure-notification `if` block, the script executed:
+```zsh
+status=$?
+```
+In `zsh`, `status` is a built-in **read-only** variable (equivalent to `$?`). Assigning to `status` is a fatal shell error (`/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`), which terminated the script on line 19 before it could reach lines 21–24 (`"$NOTIFY" "nightly review FAILED ..."`). As a result, `claude` failed first, and `zsh` killed the failure reporter immediately afterward.
+
+---
+
+## Fixes Applied
+
+1. **`Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`**
+   - Added `<key>USER</key><string>vk</string>` under `EnvironmentVariables` so `claude` can access its Keychain credentials under `launchd`.
+2. **`bin/nightly-review.zsh`**
+   - Replaced `status=$?` with `rc=$?` (and `$status` with `$rc`) so `zsh` does not abort after `claude` exits.
+   - Piped the prompt to `claude -p` via stdin (`print -r -- "$PROMPT" | claude -p --output-format text > "$OUT"`).
+   - Placed the failure notification (`"$NOTIFY" ...`) immediately at the top of the failure path (`if [ $rc -ne 0 ]`).
+   - Added run duration tracking (`SECONDS=0` / `duration=$SECONDS`), logged each run's outcome and duration, and verified that `$OUT` is non-empty (`if [ ! -s "$OUT" ]`) so an empty output file is also caught and reported as a failure.
